 on nourishing my body so i make sure to  eat lots of greens and especially  nutrient rich greens so basically kale  over lettuce for example and more  benefits of loading up on veggies is  that they're high in fiber and they can  improve your digestive flora which does  wonders for your body when it comes to  the meat department it's also really  important to choose good quality  proteins so organic grass-fed meats  thankfully we have chickens outside  which you can probably hear in the  background so i have a great supply of  organic eggs but i also still really  enjoy my favorite vegan pea protein  powder by sun warrior because it's keto  friendly no soy or whey and it's a  really high quality pea protein plus  it's super delicious with no chalky  aftertaste for fats i like to follow dr  burke's advice most of the time and that  is to make sure that your proteins are  included together with your fats so  basically that means something like a  crunchy bacon a fatty salmon an egg with  the yolk but i also really love avocados  so i enjoy the heck out of those bad  boys i usually have two meals per day  and i allow myself one sweet tasting  snack somewhere in between and it's  usually either of these two things a  coffee latte with some unsweetened pea  milk unflavored collagen powder coconut  creamer or coconut milk and a packet of  sweetener  check out this latte art you guys  i could be a barista  gorgeous  or my next favorite which is a delicious  berry smoothie i add just a little bit  of raspberries which is the only fruit  that i am allowing myself because it's  very low in neck carbs a tablespoon of  flax seeds  unflavored collagen  and of course my favorite pea protein  powder in the flavor berry by a sun  warrior no stevia or any kind of  sweetener needed for this one because  it's already sweet enough i love this i  actually have tried some of the like  alternative keto recipes to carb things  i recently made a flat bread out of  coconut flour and psyllium husk powder  which was actually pretty good but i  haven't really made them since then  because the way i see it is this i am  eating during a short window and i'm  already restricting myself to the things  that i eat so i want to make sure that i  nourish my body as much as possible and  so if i get full on coconut flour then i  think that kind of defeats the purpose  at least for me anyway but it is nice to  know that you also have these other  options so that you're not feeling like  you can't have anything or if you have a  craving then there are alternatives that  you can have i know that some people use  fat bombs which are basically like a fat  loaded snack or a drink to try to reduce  hunger so that it makes it more  manageable as they transition into the  keto diet but i personally don't really  recommend doing it for an extended  period of time if what you're trying to  do is doing it for weight loss because  coming from somebody that has done  intermittent fasting for a long period  of time i mean years on and off i've  just i've come to learn that hunger is  something that doesn't just accumulate  and get worse over time that really it  comes and goes in waves because of  hormones it's a hormonal process and so  as you learn to kind of manage that and  maneuver that it becomes more manageable  and then food becomes something that's  pleasing that's meant to nourish your  body as opposed to just kind of an  addiction or eating out of plain boredom  or eating out of emotion because i was  definitely an emotional eater in the  past let me know am i the only one have  you ever overeaten because of an emotion  you were feeling let's talk about that  dreaded keto flu i feel like everybody  talks about this but i felt like i  developed a pretty good grasp for it  when i tried a 48-hour water only fast  by putting my body under unnecessary  torture i learned a few things that  helped me to avoid the keto flu  altogether in these last three weeks so  keep these things in mind and hopefully  they will help you the first thing is  that if you pair keto with intermittent  fasting because of the boosted effects  on your metabolism don't just drink  water for hydration drink green tea or  matcha which is loaded with antioxidants  vitamins and minerals and electrolytes  if you're feeling hungry grab yourself  one of these first also for the first  week or so i was urinating a lot i mean  i was urinating like i was nine months  pregnant you guys and so i did some  research on it because i thought this  was weird and i came to realize that  it's actually common as your body starts  to transition into fat burning mode and  so to avoid dehydration i have been  adding a lot of salt to my meals and  actually this is something that was to  me pretty exciting because i always  avoided salt thinking that i was doing  the healthy option but i think that this  has definitely helped me to avoid those  dehydration symptoms and the headaches  and just those symptoms in general and  i've also been very diligent to take my  supplements seriously because again this  is not about hurting my body to achieve  a certain goal it's about nourishing my  body and giving it sort of a reset  period so i really like to add  nutritional use to really most anything  like my sauteed veggies or scrambled  eggs because it's a good source of  vitamin b i'm also taking a multivitamin  a vitamin d3 omegas and a good quality  probiotic the one that i use is by mega  food and it's called mega flora i am no  doctor to recommend this to you but  there is a huge link between your gut  health and your body's overall health  and so i've spent hours and hours trying  to find the right probiotic because a  lot of them are so expensive they have  such a high price tag but yet they have  all these strains that are really  actually not doing your body any good  and so i tried to find a good compromise  for me that was an okay prize that also  had some strains that would be helpful  for my body i am really trying to heal  my body inside out and so personally i  view it as an important part of my daily  routine so now let's talk about what i'm  not eating because i can see where this  can kind of get counterproductive and  keep in mind that this is just what is  working for me the first thing that i  want to mention is dairy because a lot  of people really enjoy adding cheese and  creams and all these things on their  keto diet but for me i have found that  all those sorts of things are just  highly inflammatory they flare up my  eczema they make me bloated and have  other gi side effects and so yeah no no  milk and cheese and all those things for  me no thank you i do eat my organic eggs  as i mentioned but as far as like milk  and cheese and those sorts of things  it's plant-based so basically like  unsweetened female almond milk or  coconut milk which is high in fat so  it's perfect for keto anyway i also am  avoiding gmos soy because of its effects  on estrogen and most of it is gmo anyway  and whey because away tends to spike  insulin and remember the goal is to keep  that insulin down i'm also personally  avoiding all those prepackaged keto  snacks like the keto cookies and cereals  and whatever else is out there because  again my focus is nourishing my body and  so even if it means i have to cook a  little bit more i don't think it really  necessarily means that i have to spend a  lot of time with it because i could just  have a salad that has avocado or boiled  eggs and there you go i can just do that  really quickly and i don't really need  the prepackaged snacks so i don't need  you keto cookies and when it comes to  meats i eat meats with no nitrates  preservatives or sugars added because  the first time i was really going  looking for meats for keto i realized  that there are a lot of meats that have  sugars in them which you'd be surprised  so read the labels on them because  they're sneaky and it's also important  to know that when it comes to those zero  calorie sweeteners they're not all the  same i was about to purchase a stevia  that in the ingredients list had  dextrose well dextrose increases your  insulin levels and so that kind of  defeats the purpose i personally use  erythritol it just happens to be what i  found at my grocery store it's of course  not as good as the real deal but it'll  do when i want the occasional coffee  latte and last but not least why am i  loving it so far oh i really don't want  to give it all away because i'm going to  be filming a full video on all those  details later on but i'm really excited  that i have taken this as seriously as i  have because  for the first time in a long time i have  a flat belly with no bloating and my  skin i'm just really excited to show you  the before and after pictures and i've  had a lot of other side effects as well  that i'm really excited to share with  you so if you're interested in that make  sure you hit that subscribe button and  the notification bell so that you won't  miss when it's out or miss any of my  other videos i hope that you found this  video helpful i thank you so much for  watching and i can't wait to hear from  you in the comments until next time bye

